Hi Violet,

I would use all of the location classes, and not just the best ones, unless there is some relation with outliers. The poorer location classes will be assigned proportionally larger errors in the model.
Yes, the bias corrections and uncertainty estimates allow for such comparisons.
>From the red points in the periodogram, the variogram oscillations could be largely from periodic missingness in the data. Less movement at night could be another factor, but some of that could be sample size.
When the errors are substantial in the model, this often happens and I haven't been able to figure out how to solve it, but some of the variogram variance is due to location error here.
Best,
Chris

